<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuania to sign loans for highway projects.</title>
<headline>Lithuania to sign loans for highway projects.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania is set to sign almost $50 million in loans with international lenders for two major highway projects, the president's office said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>The statement said that President Algirdas Brazauskas had signed a decree empowering Finance Minister Algimantas Krizhinauskas to sign a $23.2 million agreement with the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development and a $6.7 million agreement with the Nordic Investment Bank for the Via Baltica project.</p>
<p>The project would link Helsinki to Warsaw via the Baltic capitals of Tallinn and Riga and Lithuania's second city of Kaunas.</p>
<p>The president's office also said that Lithuania would sign a $19 million loan with the World Bank to improve the Vilnius-Kaunas highway and roads in the country's two largest cities.</p>
</text>
